---
// The splice pipeline from "The pivot", as a Mermaid flowchart. The diagram is
// pre-rendered to SVG at author time (one per theme) and inlined here, so no
// mermaid.js runtime ships to readers. To regenerate after editing the graph,
// see src/assets/diagrams/splice-pipeline.gen.mjs and re-run mermaid-cli.
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/splice-pipeline-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/splice-pipeline-dark.svg?raw';
---

<figure class="post-diagram">
  <div class="diagram light" set:html={lightSvg} aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="diagram dark" set:html={darkSvg} aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {/* Text alternative for screen readers + the failure the diagram can't say. */}
  <p class="sr-only">
    The master splits at Demucs into an instrumental stem and a vocal stem. The
    vocal stem goes through librosa onset detection to find the chant slots.
    Separately, the replacement name is synthesized by Chirp 3 HD, then
    time-stretched, pitched, bandpassed and clipped into name clips. The slots
    and the clips meet at the splice, which is remixed with the instrumental
    stem into the festival edit.
  </p>

  <p class="verdict">
    <span class="chip ok">✓ the name is clear</span>
    <span class="chip bad">✗ prosody reads as narration, not chant</span>
  </p>

  <figcaption>
    The splice pipeline I hand-built. Every stage did its job. The merge at the
    bottom is where it fell down: clear words, wrong instrument.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .post-diagram {
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0;
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg) var(--space-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--accent) 2.5%, var(--surface));
  }

  .diagram {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  /* mermaid stamps an inline max-width; let the SVG breathe to the column */
  .diagram :global(svg) {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 440px;
    height: auto;
  }
  /* The node labels are fixed-width foreignObjects measured at render time.
     The site's global ss01/cv11 features render Inter a hair wider on-page, so
     the text overflows and clips. Match the measured metrics and stop clipping. */
  .diagram :global(foreignObject),
  .diagram :global(.nodeLabel),
  .diagram :global(.edgeLabel),
  .diagram :global(.labelBkg) {
    overflow: visible;
    font-feature-settings: normal;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .dark {
    display: none;
  }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .light {
    display: none;
  }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .dark {
    display: flex;
  }

  .verdict {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-sm);
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .chip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .chip.ok {
    color: var(--color-status-green);
  }
  .chip.bad {
    color: var(--color-status-red);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 16, 'SOFT' 60, 'WONK' 0;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    text-wrap: balance;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>
